
Staff order assign functionality


Changes Made to application/controllers/Leads.php:
Updated get_next_staff() function (lines 1389-1518):
Step 1-3: Existing logic to get campaign and current shift

Step 4 - NEW: Fallback logic

If no staff found in the current shift, the system now fetches all staff assigned to the campaign (any shift)
This ensures leads are always assigned even when no one is on duty in the current shift
Step 5: Filter out staff with meta_force_stop = 'Y'

Step 6 - UPDATED: Language filtering (replaced old tamil_speak checkbox)

Extracts language from lead data
Looks up language ID from languages table (supports both language name and code)
Filters staff who speak the lead's language using the new staff_languages table
Falls back to all filtered staff if no language match found
Step 7-8: Existing round-robin distribution logic

Gets last assigned staff
Distributes to next staff in the filtered list using round-robin
How It Works:
Shift-based assignment: First tries to assign to staff in the current shift
Fallback: If no staff in shift, expands to all staff assigned to the campaign
Language matching: Within the available staff, filters by language if lead has language data
Round-robin: Distributes leads evenly among eligible staff
Example Flow:
Lead arrives with language "Tamil"
System checks current shift (e.g., 9 AM - 6 PM)
Gets staff in that shift for the campaign
Filters out staff with meta_force_stop
Filters for Tamil-speaking staff
Assigns to next Tamil-speaking staff in round-robin order
If no Tamil speakers in shift, falls back to all Tamil speakers in campaign
The system is now ready to handle Meta leads with intelligent shift and language-based distribution.





